== Notes ==
* Slowing Gurdy Jr. will, for the most part, render her charge attack useless.
* {{Dlc|nr}} [[Piercing tears]] lack knockback and cannot be used to divert or stop Gurdy Jr.'s charge attack.
* If Gurdy Jr. is [[fear]]ed/[[confusion|stunned]] during her charge attack after the effect wears off, she will immediately charge at Isaac.
* Gurdy Jr's charge attack has no telegraphing, making it very dangerous to stay close due to the lack of a warning.

== Trivia ==
* Gurdy Jr. was added in the ''Wrath of The Lamb'' DLC for the original ''The Binding of Isaac''.
** Gurdy Jr. from ''Wrath of the Lamb'' is larger than Gurdy Jr. in Rebirth.
** In the original game, Gurdy Jr. could be encountered in the {{s|Cellar}}.
*** Also in the original game, in Chapter 2, Gurdy Jr. could only be encountered in The {{s|Catacombs}}, while in Rebirth, she can be encountered in all environments of Chapter 2 (in The {{s|Caves}}, The {{s|Catacombs}}, and The {{s|Flooded Caves}}).
* Gurdy Jr. appears to be the second stage of the "Gurdy" boss line, with the first stage as {{e|Gurglings}}, third as {{e|Gurdy}}, and final as {{e|Mama Gurdy}}.
* Gurdy Jr. is female.<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20120831111557/http://www.formspring.me/EdmundM/q/341049925531883948</ref>
* Edmund McMillen has referred to the double Gurdy Jr. champion room in an interview as "double Gurditration".

